From f0823a753718bd183f151df23095aa7e792890ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leo Yu-Chi Liang <ycliang@andestech.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jul 2024 16:36:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/53] andes: cpu: Support network functionality on
 noncoherent bitmaps (#99)

There are several ways to support network on noncoherent bitmap in u-boot proper:
1. Disable cache (For a25 noncoherent bitmap)
2. Set MSB bit + flush/invalidate cache (For ax25 noncoherent bitmap)
3. Set PPMA + flush/invalidate cache (For noncoherent bitmap with PPMA support)

We ported SYS_HAS_NONCACHED_MEMORY to RISC-V archictecture
and implement 2 & 3 via this u-boot config.

First initialize an memory area with their attribute set to noncacheable (through PPMA or MSB bit).
Allocate from this memory area when noncahced memory is needed through noncached_alloc API.

Signed-off-by: Leo Yu-Chi Liang <ycliang@andestech.com>

Reviewed-on: https://gitea.andestech.com/RD-SW/u-boot.official/pulls/99
Reviewed-by: randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
Reviewed-by: Mina Hui-Min Chou <minachou@andestech.com>
